The nested's Aquamarine (gate/host.sh applies this to the fork's flake.lock
pin). CWaylandOutput::commit() rebuilt the swapchain options from scratch,
dropping the consumer's scanout flag that Hyprland's updateSwapchain() sets
before each state commit: every frame reallocated the swapchain twice, and
next() handed out blank buffers that claim age 3, so pixels outside a
frame's damage (a static shadow) presented black. Drop this file once the
pin carries the fix (the build then fails to apply it).

--- a/src/backend/Wayland.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/Wayland.cpp
@@ -674,7 +674,10 @@
         return true;
     }
 
-    if (!swapchain->reconfigure(SSwapchainOptions{.length = swapchain->currentOptions().length, .size = pixelSize, .format = format})) {
+    auto options   = swapchain->currentOptions();
+    options.size   = pixelSize;
+    options.format = format;
+    if (!swapchain->reconfigure(options)) {
         backend->backend->log(AQ_LOG_ERROR, std::format("Output {}: pending state rejected: swapchain failed reconfiguring", name));
         return false;
     }
